"""Task 244: a CALCULATE filter inside a column added by SUMMARIZE, under an outer CALCULATE, and the taken-branch rule for number-type tests of a conditional over a Variant iterator.

Every expected answer is a live Power BI answer on the Facts table of tools.dax_oracle_diff (6 rows: Sales, Quantity, Region, Note), or on a second table (SECOND_ROWS),
a third (THIRD_ROWS) or a fourth (FOURTH_ROWS, with twin rows).

The measured rules, in plain words:
  * An extension column of SUMMARIZE (Facts, group-by columns, "s", CALCULATE(...)) is evaluated on the group seen as a set of whole rows of the source table:
    every column the group does not name is the set of values those rows hold.  An explicit column filter in the extension replaces the filter on its column and the group
    narrows to the rows that still match it on the other columns (the group's own value of a filtered column is dropped); ALL, REMOVEFILTERS and VALUES behave the same.
    PART_A_ROW (CALCULATE(SUMX(SUMMARIZE(Facts,Facts[Region],Facts[Quantity],"s",CALCULATE(SUM(Facts[Sales]),Facts[Quantity]>1)),[s]*2),Facts[Quantity]>1)) is 66 in Power BI;
    the engine said 92.  ALLSELECTED of a column inside such a column re-derives the group from the remaining group-by columns.
  * Stays refused (unsure => refused): a CALCULATE filter on several columns inside an iterator over a group-by column inside such a column, ALLSELECTED of several tables,
    ALLSELECTED after a KEEPFILTERS filter on the same table, ALLSELECTED of a group-by column beside a filter on another group-by column.
  * A number-type test (ISINTEGER, ISINT64, ISDOUBLE, ISDECIMAL, ISCURRENCY) of an IF / SWITCH / COALESCE / IFERROR with a SUMX, MAXX or MINX branch over a Variant column
    (ADDCOLUMNS, SELECTCOLUMNS, SUMMARIZE, SUMMARIZECOLUMNS ...) is typed by the branch that is taken; the engine answers it when the Variant column is built by IF and COALESCE
    (or an IFERROR whose fallback is a number).  AVERAGEX, an IFERROR with a text fallback, SWITCH, SELECTEDVALUE, and the set/join builders over a Variant stay refused.
"""
